# Walnut (ps3-desktop): loop devices are not mounted by the desktop's automounter. walnut-data
# (Walnut Games' "Add game files...") opens a disc image with udisksctl loop-setup and mounts it
# itself; the desktop's gvfs/udisks automount raced it and pcmanfm showed "Device /dev/loopN is
# already mounted at ..." in an error dialog. An image opened from the file manager is still mounted
# (by an explicit request, which UDISKS_AUTO does not affect).
SUBSYSTEM=="block", KERNEL=="loop[0-9]*", ENV{UDISKS_AUTO}="0"
